==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael help [<command> | <topic>] [--json]

Read command help and cross-command guidance.

Commands take precedence over topics. Help works without a connection or saved
login. `raphael help <x>`, `raphael <x> --help` and `raphael <x> -h` print the
same page, as text or, with --json, as the same document.

`raphael help reference` prints every page in one stream.

Options:
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael help create
  raphael help reference
  raphael help --json search

Prints:
  Help text. With --json, one document {"ok":true,"command":"help",...}:
  commands, topics, examples, exitCodes and errorCodes for the root page and
  reference, definition for a command, topic for a topic. `raphael help output`
  describes it.

Next: raphael help reference
